@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<article>
    <header class="mb-3">
        <h1 class="fw-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">Last updated: @DateTime.Now.ToString("d MMMM yyyy", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.GetCultureInfo("en-US"))</p>
    </header>

    <p>
        Geekspace is an educational project built to demonstrate web application development
        concepts, including user authentication, database-driven content, and community
        discussion features. This page explains what information the platform collects, how
        it is used, and the choices available to you.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account information:</strong> when you register, we store your email address and a securely hashed version of your password. We never store your password in plain text.</li>
            <li><strong>Content you create:</strong> comments, replies, and votes (likes/dislikes) you post are stored and linked to your account so they can be displayed, edited, or removed by you or an administrator.</li>
            <li><strong>Optional security data:</strong> if you choose to enable TOTP (authenticator app) two-factor authentication, we store the shared secret key required to verify your login codes.</li>
            <li><strong>Local preferences:</strong> your light/dark theme choice is stored in your browser's local storage, not on our servers, and never leaves your device.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>Information you provide is used only to operate the platform, specifically to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Authenticate you and maintain your login session.</li>
            <li>Display your username alongside comments and replies you post.</li>
            <li>Enforce role-based permissions (User, Admin, Root) across the site.</li>
            <li>Allow administrators to moderate content in accordance with the site's community rules.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties, and we do not run advertising or third-party analytics on this site.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">3. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            Geekspace uses a single essential cookie to keep you signed in between requests.
            This cookie is required for the site to function and does not track you across
            other websites. No advertising or third-party tracking cookies are used.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">4. Data Storage</h2>
        <p>
            All data is stored in a local SQLite database associated with this application.
            No data is transmitted to or processed by any external cloud service, and no data
            is shared outside of the Geekspace platform.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">5. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>You may edit or delete your own comments and replies at any time.</li>
            <li>You may request that an administrator delete your account and associated data.</li>
            <li>You may enable or disable two-factor authentication at any time from your account settings.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">6. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            Geekspace is intended for users capable of independently creating an account and is
            not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
            children.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            As this is an educational project, this policy may be updated as new features are
            added to the platform. Continued use of the site after changes indicates acceptance
            of the updated policy.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="h4">8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            This is a student coursework project and is not a commercial service. Questions
            about this policy can be directed to the site administrator through the account
            management options available after logging in.
        </p>
    </section>
</article>
